[docs/engine.md > Colliders and radii] - **free objects** (`+0xa9 & 8`): `PHYS_AttachObjectCollider` (`0x40be46`), radius **50**, mass 10;

[NAME] Descriptive name. Gives a walker a collision sphere of radius +0x10c; its ZZZZZ child node is the foot marker (+0x84); ZZZZZ and BASSIN01 nodes are hidden. Sources: analysis engine.md physics 2026-09-26; blind review (medium); adjudicated AGREE. Facts (tools/check_names.py): str:ZZZZZ; str:BASSIN01; str:can't create collision sphere; call:0045744c.

[DOCS_SYNC]
[docs/engine.md > Colliders and radii] - **walkers** (`+0xa9 & 2`): `PHYS_AttachActorCollider` (`0x40bedb`), both sides, radius actor `+0x10c`; the model's `ZZZZZ` node is the foot marker (`+0x84`) and is hidden along with `BASSIN01`;

